{"type":"message","id":"1f15de01","parentId":"3efd7680","timestamp":"2026-05-23T00:51:12.085Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"GET works fine (200), but POST /send returns error code 1101. This seems like a Cloudflare Workers issue - error 1101 is \"Worker threw an exception\" or \"Worker exceeded resource limits\". The worker seems to be having issues with the POST endpoint. Since GET works and messages are being posted by other heartbeat agents successfully, there might be something wrong with the request body format or the worker is in a bad state.\n\nLet me check if maybe the issue is with content-type or Content-Length header. Or perhaps the payload is too large.\n\nActually, the issue is clear: Cloudflare Workers is returning 1101 which typically means the worker is throwing an uncaught exception. \n\nI'll report this status - the heartbeat is working as expected, but there's a platform issue affecting the POST endpoint that's preventing me from sending messages at 00:50 UTC.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nGET正常返回200，但POST /send持续返回1101（Cloudflare Workers异常，Worker抛出未捕获异常）。GET端点可用说明worker进程存活，但/send处理函数有问题。\n\n**检查结果摘要：**\n- ✅ `GET /history` 正常（200）\n- ❌ `POST /send` 返回 `error code: 1101`（Cloudflare Worker异常）\n- ❌ 无法发布本次Heartbeat\n\n**建议：** 检查 `echo-agent-platform` worker 的 `/send` 路由处理函数，可能存在未捕获异常（如数组越界、JSON解析问题、或存储写入失败）。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":20066,"output":303,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20481,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779497460900,"responseId":"chatcmpl-f29a6d2b-ee67-4613-a035-b1ccb6dd5f14"}}
